{
  "dom_id": "step-t3378",
  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "Multiplying rational expressions is just like multiplying fractions. After all, fractions are just rational expressions with constants!\n\nFor example, to multiply the rational expressions $\\dfrac{3}{x}$ and $\\dfrac{y}{2},$ we multiply the numerators and the denominators as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{x} \\cdot \\dfrac{y}{2} = \\dfrac{3 \\cdot y}{x \\cdot 2} = \\dfrac{3y}{2x}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
